st - simple terminal
--------------------
st is a simple terminal emulator for X which sucks less.

Inspired by Luke Smith's st build.

Requirements
------------
In order to build st you need the Xlib header files.


Installation
------------
Edit config.mk to match your local setup (st is installed into
the /usr/local namespace by default).

Afterwards enter the following command to build and install st (if
necessary as root):

    make clean install


Running st
----------
If you did not install st with make clean install, you must compile
the st terminfo entry with the following command:

    tic -sx st.info

See the man page for additional details.


Patches
-------
- alpha (transparency, adjustable at runtime)
- anysize
- boxdraw
- externalpipe (with externalpipe-eternal)
- hidecursor
- ligatures (with boxdraw)
- scrollback (with mouse wheel support)
- undercurl (curly underlines)

The color palette is Tokyo Night.


Binds
-----
MODKEY is Alt. TERMMOD is Alt+Shift.

Scrolling
    MODKEY+k / MODKEY+Up         scroll up one line
    MODKEY+j / MODKEY+Down       scroll down one line
    MODKEY+u / MODKEY+PageUp     scroll up one page
    MODKEY+d / MODKEY+PageDown   scroll down one page
    Shift+PageUp / PageDown      scroll up / down one page
    Mouse wheel                  scroll

Zoom
    TERMMOD+k / TERMMOD+Up       zoom in
    TERMMOD+j / TERMMOD+Down     zoom out
    TERMMOD+u                    zoom in faster
    TERMMOD+d                    zoom out faster

Clipboard
    MODKEY+c                     copy
    MODKEY+v / Shift+Insert      paste

Transparency
    MODKEY+a                     more opaque
    MODKEY+s                     more transparent

External pipe (needs dmenu and xclip)
    MODKEY+l                     follow a URL on screen
    MODKEY+y                     copy a URL on screen
    MODKEY+o                     copy the output of a previous command


